---
import NarrativePage from '../components/NarrativePage.astro'
const page = {
  "title": "Veqtor Workspace — Supported use and limitations",
  "description": "Current platform, document, editing and saving limits for Veqtor Workspace, including tracked changes and Word review.",
  "eyebrow": "Limitations",
  "heading": "Know what to check before relying on a result.",
  "lede": "Start with a copy, give a specific instruction and review the saved document in Word.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "platform",
      "title": "Mac and a connected assistant",
      "body": [
        "The current Workspace runs on macOS and needs a separate AI assistant. It is not a Word add-in or a live view of an open Word window. A public Workspace installer is not available yet; the installation page describes the preview connection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "documents",
      "title": "Word is the main workflow",
      "body": [
        "The demonstrated workflow uses Word documents and text-based PDFs as supporting material. Scanned documents need separate text recognition. Do not assume that every file format or every Word feature has been validated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "changes",
      "title": "Ask for the editing mode you need",
      "body": [
        "Tracked changes are not automatically applied to every task. Ask for them explicitly. Also specify whether you want comments, a clean version, acceptance of existing revisions, or a reading-only response. Check that the result matches your request."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "word",
      "title": "Check the result in Word",
      "body": [
        "Complex tables, fields, numbering, drawings, existing revisions and comments need particular attention. Optional diagnostics do not test Word’s rendering or accept/reject behavior. A rendered preview may paginate differently and depends on a separately available renderer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "concurrency",
      "title": "Save first and avoid simultaneous edits",
      "body": [
        "The assistant reads the last saved file, not unsaved Word changes. The save check detects changes already written to disk; it is not a live lock across applications. Reopen the file after the assistant saves it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "copies",
      "title": "Copies and logs remain locally",
      "body": [
        "Working copies, snapshots and logs may remain in private application storage until removed. They can contain confidential text. Use your own document retention and backup practices."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "path": "/limitations",
  "linkSection": {
    "eyebrow": "Related",
    "title": "More about working with documents",
    "links": [
      {
        "href": "/security",
        "title": "Local files and data handling"
      },
      {
        "href": "/docs",
        "title": "Technical documentation"
      },
      {
        "href": "/product",
        "title": "What Workspace does"
      }
    ]
  }
}
---
<NarrativePage {...page} />
